Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(win32): normalize paths at permission boundaries

This PR resolves remaining Windows path-matching bugs without requiring a massive architectural rewrite of the backend's native Node.js path handling.

Changes:
- Wildcard.match: Normalizes strings to POSIX / immediately prior to Regex evaluation. This ensures opencode.json permission rules match correctly regardless of whether the AI or OS provides a backslash \ or forward slash /.
- external-directory.ts: Ensures the generated glob patterns sent to the UI for user approval use forward slashes for cross-platform consistency in saved rules.
- bash.test.ts: Modifies the rm tmpfile test to target a nested directory, preventing false-positive test failures when run in MSYS/Cygwin environments that map Windows temp directories to virtual /tmp mounts.
- Updated associated tests to reflect the normalized output formats.
